course: dictionary
lesson: 2215
title: Courage
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Courage is the ability to do something that frightens you or is difficult, even when you feel afraid. It is another word for bravery. Courage is a noun, and you cannot count it: we say "some courage", not "three courages".
explain: Courage does not mean having no fear. «Being frightened does not make someone a coward; courage means doing the right thing while feeling afraid.» You can shake, feel scared and still speak up. The courage is in acting anyway.
explain: Courage shows up at school too. «When friends want to leave someone out, invite them in; it takes courage to be kind when others aren't.» The clue is "when others aren't": the brave choice goes against the crowd. Telling the truth and admitting a mistake also take courage.
explain: In danger, courage does not mean taking silly risks. The brave and sensible choice is often to get help from a grown-up. Ask yourself: what is the courageous thing to do here, and is it safe?
fact: Courage is a noun, and it is uncountable: you cannot say "a courage" or "two courages".
fact: Courage means the ability to do something that frightens you or is difficult, even when you feel afraid: bravery.
fact: «The courage of your convictions» means being brave enough to do what you believe is right.
fact: Useful phrases: have the courage to, take courage, pluck up the courage, lose courage, an act of courage.
fact: In stories, heroes face dragons, storms or bullies, and courage is what helps them through.
exercise: «Being frightened does not make someone a coward; courage means doing the right thing while feeling afraid.» What is courage in this sentence? | Running away fast | *Doing the right thing even while afraid | Shouting loudly at others | Never feeling scared
exercise: Which phrase means to find the bravery to start? | be counted in courages | lose courage | have no fear at all | *pluck up the courage
exercise: Which sentence about courage is correct? | We say "two courages" | *We say "some courage" | We say "a courage" | We say "courages" for many brave people
test: «It takes courage to be kind when others aren't.» What does courage mean here? | *Bravery to do the right thing | Good luck | Loudness | Silliness
test: In danger, what does courage ask you to do? | Take the biggest risk you can find | *Get help from a grown-up instead of taking silly risks | Hide and say nothing | Wander off alone
exam: Which sentence shows that courage is not the same as having no fear? | «Respect is earned by effort, skill, honesty, kindness and courage.» | «Virtues are good habits such as honesty and courage.» | *«Being frightened does not make someone a coward; courage means doing the right thing while feeling afraid.» | «Courage is a noun.»
